  "d2: 🍽️ Nadia sets the sharing basket down by the fire instead of the pantry. \"Full shelves don't need my little more.\"",
  "d3: 🍽️ Elif taps the pantry's fullest jar. \"More than we can eat before it turns. Rendering fat instead — the lamps won't fill themselves.\"",
  "d3: 🍽️ Nadia carries the day's surplus to the pantry door, thinks better of it, and turns back to the fire. \"It'll only rot in there. We eat.\"",
  "d4: 🍽️ Scott weighs the day's basket against the pantry shelves and puts it down. \"Enough. Carving bowls instead — we're down to the cracked ones.\"",
  "d4: 🍽️ Brian carries the day's surplus to the pantry door, thinks better of it, and turns back to the fire. \"It'll only rot in there. We eat.\"",
  "d5: 🍽️ Vasyl checks the pantry before heading out, then hangs back. \"Shelves are full to bursting. Patching the boots today.\"",
  "d5: 🍽️ Nadia leaves the surplus by the fire for whoever's hungry. \"The pantry can't take it. We can.\"",
  "d6: 🍽️ Nadia stands in the pantry doorway a moment. \"Look at all this. Tending the fire today — someone ought to keep the stories.\"",
  "d6: 🍽️ Elif looks at the full shelves and waves off the day's share. \"No more into the store — we eat at the fire, and the shelves keep.\"",
  "d7: 🍽️ David takes one look at the full shelves and unshoulders the pack. \"Leave the wild standing. Hauling water for the cistern.\"",
  "d7: 🍽️ Vasyl leaves the surplus by the fire for whoever's hungry. \"The pantry can't take it. We can.\"",
  "d8: 🍽️ Ashanti rests a hand on the pantry door, satisfied. \"No one's going hungry this week. Sitting with the fever cases instead — someone should.\"",
